  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Point $p=\\left(\\frac{6+2}{5}, \\frac{12+2}{5}\\right)$\n$\\mathrm{p}=\\left(\\frac{8}{5}, \\frac{14}{5}\\right)$\n$p\\left(\\frac{8}{5}, \\frac{14}{5}\\right)$ lies on $2 x+y=k \\quad \\Rightarrow \\frac{16}{5}+\\frac{14}{5}=k \\quad \\Rightarrow k=\\frac{30}{5}=6$",
    "image": null
